// _urlInt(name, dflt, ok) — read an INTEGER world parameter from the page URL at module load.
//   THE SHARED SHAPE for every such parameter (G, SUB, CPU_SUB): the value is read ONCE, here, and baked into
//   the world program every peer builds — so the initial state is identical on all of them BY CONSTRUCTION,
//   exactly as if it were a hand-edited constant. That is what makes a URL parameter admissible where a boot
//   VERB is not: a verb fires at a peer-local moment and a joiner would restore mid-transition.
//   `ok` VALIDATES, and it is not optional politeness — an out-of-range value would produce a world no other
//   peer can build, so a malformed URL must fall back to the default rather than invent one.
