    //   'sub' and it does not work"). URLSearchParams.get() IS case-sensitive, so ?sub=16 misses "SUB" and
    //   falls through to the default — SILENTLY, which is exactly why it read as "the parameter is ignored".
    //   Anything that normalises a pasted link (a chat client, an editor, a browser autocomplete, typing it by
    //   hand) can lowercase the query and every one of these parameters quietly stops working.
    //   So match on the lowercased KEY. The names stay upper-case in docs and in the HUD because that is what
    //   they are called in the source; the reader simply does not care how they were typed.
